    "thread_id": "thread_37926b434be9",
    "query": "What is the Section 80C deduction limit for FY 2024-25?",
    "financial_year": "2024-25",
    "draft_answer": "**Section 80C deduction limit for FY 2024‑25**\n\n- The maximum amount that can be claimed under **section 80C** (together with the related limits under sections 80CCC and 80CCD(1)) is **₹ 1,50,000**. If the aggregate of these deductions exceeds ₹ 1,50,000 the return is rejected [C1].\n\n- This ceiling applies when the **old tax regime** is selected.  \n  - Under the **new tax regime (section 115BAC)**, deductions under section 80C (and the related sections 80CCC, 80CCD(1) etc.) are not permitted; the system enforces a zero‑limit for these items [C4][C6][C7].\n\n---\n\n*LexIndia provides legal information, not professional tax advice.*",
    "final_answer": "**Section 80C deduction limit for FY 2024‑25**\n\n- The maximum amount that can be claimed under **section 80C** (together with the related limits under sections 80CCC and 80CCD(1)) is **₹ 1,50,000**. If the aggregate of these deductions exceeds ₹ 1,50,000 the return is rejected [C1].\n\n- This ceiling applies when the **old tax regime** is selected.  \n  - Under the **new tax regime (section 115BAC)**, deductions under section 80C (and the related sections 80CCC, 80CCD(1) etc.) are not permitted; the system enforces a zero‑limit for these items [C4][C6][C7].\n\n---\n\n*LexIndia provides legal information, not professional tax advice.*",
